1. Problem Statement
Process student marks across multiple subjects, validate subject-wise pass cutoffs (>=40), apply conditional grace marks (up to 5 marks) for candidates missing pass criteria in at most one subject, and prevent moderation from exceeding maximum subject marks (100).

2. Objectives
•	Evaluate pass criteria per subject and across aggregate marks.
•	Apply grace marks strictly when eligibility conditions are met.
•	Ensure capped moderation results do not exceed 100.

3. Assumptions
•	Maximum score per subject is 100.
•	Subject pass mark is 40.
•	Grace marks apply only if exactly one subject has score between 35 and 39.

4. Algorithm
1. Read student list with marks in 3 subjects.
2. Count subjects with marks < 40.
3. If fail count == 1 and failing mark >= 35, add required grace marks (up to 5) to bring score to 40.
4. Recalculate pass status.
5. If all subjects >= 40, mark as PASS, else FAIL.
6. Cap all subject scores at 100.
